[45.42806, "o", "== due\r\n0 due; 2 scheduled, next at 2026-10-11T09:34:16.100Z\r\n== island: Ship the fuse change\r\nSeat island. Activation is spread from search seeds along links. It is not a relevance rank.\r\nNot fired: fewer than two seeds that two scorers agreed on, so firing would wire the wrong links.\r\nweak island: 0 seeds two scorers agreed on; read it as the pack's best-connected cluster, not as what the cue is about; it will not fire\r\n1.000\tseed\t9393272149d5b666cfc33700cc089b4d\ttoday\tRun cargo test before every push.\r\n0.500\tseed\tcf8c6150c580c2e777f196744cc2d32b\ttoday\tNever force push to main. Open a pull request instead.\r\n== blockers\r\nnone open; the issue is workable\r\n== playbook\r\nsit\r\nA sitting on one issue. Name this recipe at open (`ljos sitting ISSUE --playbook sit` or `ljos playbook ISSUE sit`). The sitting prints this body before recall and holds the name until finish or release.\r\n1. Open with `ljos sitting ISSUE --playbook sit`. Read doctor, cards, due, island, this recipe, recall, timeline, claim.\r\n2. Grade due claims (`ljos gr"]
[45.428497, "o", "aded ID`).\r\n3. Do the work on this claim only. Artefacts are deeds, then `ljos deed ISSUE --add ACCESSION`. Lessons are `ljos remember` in two sentences.\r\n4. One playbook step is the whole sitting. A subagent takes this recipe and this issue; it does not resume a later phase.\r\n5. Close with `ljos finish ISSUE --lesson \"...\"`. Completing the node does not close the ticket. `ljos finish ISSUE --close` does, when the work is accepted.\r\nRunner: this same runner. Do not set a model id. A spawn hint is not a model this runner can call.\r\n== recall\r\ndemo-hreh              TODO      Ship the fuse change  (demo)\r\nInputs\r\n  (none declared: nothing blocks this and it was not bounced)\r\nProduced\r\n"]
